  "title": "Flat states exist on the whole sphere",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Flat states exist on the whole sphere. On the octahedral knot sphere K_k (every k >= 2), give each point a frame (a sublattice index mod 3 and a sign gauge mod 2) moved along lines by the plane embedding and the Kasteleyn signs. The moves compose to nothing around every three-point face and, around each of the six two-point faces (the octahedron's corners), to a sublattice turn plus a complement, which shifts labels by -1. Hence for every point z and every six disjoint paths of the line-face graph from the six triangles around z to the six corner faces, developing one constant label over the sphere cut along those paths colours every line not-all-equal except exactly one line, which passes through z (a counterclockwise vortex of the labels); re-routing the cut inside a region changes colours only inside it, and from shortest cut stars the vortex steps to each neighbour by re-routing inside radius 3.",
  "dependencies": [
    "SPHERE-COUNT-20261106-001Z"
  ],
